            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="0979" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/258: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-01-05T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 5,
                                1923—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>6. Your telegram no. 3 of January 3, 4 p.m. Considering the statement by Mr.
                    Barnes Moss, is it the feeling of the Legation that it still would be wise to
                    make such a communication to the Japanese Chargé here as the Department
                    indicated in its telegram of December 28, 4 p.m., no. 299?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
